// Aggregate on BOTH sides of a comparison (a shape the let-migration never
// produces — it only ever compares one aggregate to a literal). "More
// Transfer requests than responses in the window" = some transfers are
// still pending, expressed by comparing two counts. The left aggregate is
// parenthesized so its greedy `where` body does not swallow the `<`
// operator; the right aggregate is rightmost so it needs no
// parens.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Alert",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    (count for (t: Timepoint). where (formerly within 1h (Drupe::Action::"Transfer"::response{ requestId: _ } && tp(t)))) < count for (t: Timepoint). where (formerly within 1h (Drupe::Action::"Transfer"::request{ requestId: _ } && tp(t)))};
